  ('TL1-08','Alpine Summer',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope The L1 Alpine Summer instructor can: Observation may be done by an Outdoor Lead and manage groups on formed and marked tracks, easy access to Instructor with Alpine summer (L1). tracks or on strong navigational features above the bush line in non- technical terrain in the Tongariro National Park where snow is not Assessment normally encountered. Assessor must be The following are examples of environments that are within the scope. • Alpine Summer (L2)with Training department approval Tongariro via west ridge; • Or - NZOIA Alpine 1 Wairere Valley; Pehi Crag circuit; (Not Pehi’s traverse) Assessment is by direct observation Tama Lakes circumnavigation; Whakapapa Village ridge track and Wairere Stream loop This L1 Competency is achieved once signed Pukekaikiore via Grand Gully; - Requires L2 Steep Ground off at two sites within the scope Managment The instructor must request DM approval if venturing on a new route even with full sign off. • All trips must be predominantly within range of the radio repeater Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of ❑ No less than 10 days (4 hours duration) experience walking in the alpine Current Competence environment above the bush-line ❑ 5 additional days as leader or co-leader within the scopeL1 Field Communication • NZOIA Alpine 1 L1 Risk Management L1 • 15 Logged Instruction days in the alpine summer + Observation • Some criteria may be crossed over from Bush L1 Site 1: Site 2: S elf O b s 1 s ite 1 A ssess s ite 2 A ssess Technical Compe','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "assess1": "Assess site 1", "assess2": "Assess site 2"}',2,false),
  ('TL1-11','Alpine Winter',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope Assessment Path With this competency an instructor is able to use an ice axe and take students into non-technical terrain where there may be enough snow Observation may be done by an Outdoor cover for sliding. They are able to run a single day experience in snow Instructor with Alpine Winter (L1). to approved sites that have a low avalanche rating: o within the ski-field boundary. or Assessor: Must be a Outdoor Instructor step o places with easy access to tracks or terrain without snow 2 with Alpine Winter (L2), o easy access of the Mangatepopo valley floor. or NZOIA Alpine 1 with Training department Ice axes may be issued to students, as a walking aid, and Primary approval Anchor NOT for self-arresting. The instructor may only operate at sites that have been approved on This L1 Competency is achieved once signed off at two sites within the scope the day with consideration of the current environmental conditions The instructor must request DM approval if venturing on a new route. The instructor must request DM approval if venturing on a new route even with full sign off.. The following are examples of environments that may b','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "assess1": "Assess site 1", "assess2": "Assess site 2"}',2,false),
  ('TL1-14','Bush',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope The L1 bush instructor can: Observations Lead and manage groups on formed and marked tracks, easy access to May be done by any Instructor holding Bush tracks or on strong linear features in the bush and open terrain. Walks (L1) Comp may extend above the bush-line at low altitudes in good weather conditions and the absence of snow. This may include minor river Assessment crossings or short travel in stream-ways. Assessor must be an Local bush bashing around HOEC centre with route plan approved. • Outdoor Instructor step 2 with Bush (L2) with Training department The following are examples of environments that could be within the approval scope: ✓ Most tracks on the Hillary Outdoors local map • Or NZOIA Bush 1. ✓ Off track on Local Map “Bush bashing” – Note the M.O.W Assessment is through discussion and Bush bash has steep terrain. direct observation ✓ Silica Rapids walk, ✓ Lower Tama Lake, ✓ Whakapapaiti track. ✓ Taurewa Stream (needs fimal and assessment) Note. Can be RCC signed off as Indirect with NZOIA Leader or Equivalent, With DM approval can access maintained tracks, Common HOEC Bush tracks and local Off track, Must Seek Approval Each time. Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current Competence ❑ No less than 10 days (4 hours duration) experience bush walking with 3 Days being off Track. • NZOIA Bush 1 ❑ 5 additional days as leader or co-leader in a bush environment. • 15 Logged bush instruction days + Observation A S elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Technical Compet','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
  ('TL1-17','Overnight',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope Assessment The L1 instructor can: Observations can be done by anyone with the Lead and manage groups on bush/water/alpine camps within the local Overnight (L1) Competency. operating area within easy access of well-defined tracks. Camping may extend above the bush line in good weather conditions and the Assessor must be an absence of snow • Outdoor Instructor holding Overnight The following are examples of environments within the scope: (L1) with Training department approval ✓ Blue Gums, • or NZOIA Bush 1. ✓ Club Med, ✓ Lake Otamangakau, Assessment is by observation and discussion ✓ Marty’s ✓ TNP huts ✓ Lower Tama Lake, Marty’s ✓ Wairere Stream above Taranaki Falls Note. Can be RCC signed off as Indirect with NZOIA Overnight Endorsement or Equivalent, With DM approval can access maintained campsites or easy access campsites on the local map must seek DM Approval each time. Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of ❑ No less than 10 nights personal camping Current Competence ❑ 5 additional nights as leader or co-leader ❑ L1 Bush or L1 Summer Alpine or L1 Water craft • NZOIA Bush One • 10 Logged Instruction overnights + Observation A A S elf O b s S ite 1o r ssess S ite 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate knowledge, care and appropriate use of gear and equipment commonly used.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs", "assess1": "Assess site 1", "assess2": "Assess site 2"}',2,false),
  ('TL1-20','Alpine Winter Camp',1,'Tongariro','2024, Version 9','Scope Assessment The L1 instructor can: Assessor must hold NZOIA Alpine 1 Camp in tents at a designated camp site close to (guideline: <2 hours), or and with non-technical access to, a major track or road. A Senior Instructor with Alpine Winter Camp (L1) Designated campsites are as follows and Alpine Winter - (L2) with Training  Meads wall area above Aorangi hut: GR 208537 department approval  Lower Meads Wall area east of Happy Valley: GR 207537 Assessment is by direct observation  West of Waikato hut (in view of the hut): GR 205535  The Wairere Valley less than 1.5 km from Taranaki Falls  Lower Tama Lake  Basin behind 1409, W Ridge, Tongariro Recorded Recognition of Current Prerequisites Competence ❑ L1 Alpine winter ❑ 5 personal overnight days experience camping in the snow environment • NZOIA Alpine 1 ❑ Overnight (L1) • 15 relevant Logged overnights in Winter Alpine Camping + Full Observation A s elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r SMS Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate knowledge, care and appropriate use of gear and equipment commonly used.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
