  ('TL1-25','Rock climbing',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path ➢ The holder of this qualification can organise bouldering where the Observation/supervision can be done by an landing zone is flat and hazard free and the climbers’ feet do not Outdoor Instructor with Rock Climbing (L1) exceed a height of 1.6 metres off the ground. ➢ Can set up and manage up to 3 single pitch top rope climbs where: Assessor must hold • There is well defined access to the top rope anchors or haul • Outdoor Instructor step 2, with Rock lines. Climbing (L2) with Training • There is a pre-arranged anchor set-up. department approval • The instructor has visited the site previously and had their set • NZOIA Rock 1 up approved • Personal safety can be set up simply using an approved system. Instructor must demonstrate competence at each site Instructor must be signed as competent at each site before working Competency is achieved once signed off at solo with a group. two approved sites. Sites within the scope may include: The instructor may only operate ✓ The north end of Meads ✓ Middle Earth unsupervised at sites that have been Wall ✓ Whakapapa Gorge ✓ MOW rock wall approved. ✓ High R','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
