  ('TL2-25','Grade 2 trip leader',2,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path To be trip leader and instruct and manage inflatable kayak and Observation can be done by an instructor with L2 Kayak sit-on kayak trips from a closed kayak on grade 2. Grade 2 Trip Leader Assessor must be a Senior Instructor holding NZOIA Kayak Sites within the scope may include: 1 or Internal equivalent  Lower Tongariro from Blue Pool  Lower Tongariro From Red Hut Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current L1 Kayak Grade 2 with closed kayak endorsement Competence: 5 flat water teaching sessions • NZOIA Kayak 1 with local famil 10 personal trips on grade 2 5 days personal kayaking on grade 3 No less than 5 days as a leader or assistant leader in a closed cockpit kayak on grade 2 A Site: Lower Tongariro River s elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Coordination','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
  ('TL2-28','Upper Mangatepopo Assist',2,'Tongariro','2024, Version 9','Scope Training and assessment Path The instructor with L2 Upper Mangatepopo assist competency Observation can be done by an instructor with L2 can: competency Assist managing groups in the Upper Mangatepopo River, Upper Mangatepopo River Trip including upstream to the high point access and down through all Assessor must be a Senior Instructor with the Upper the jumps above the Mangatepopo Falls abseil. Mangatepopo Trip Leader. Assessment is by direct supervision Must Have level 1 River Safety Note: The Mangatepopo Falls Abseil is a separate L3 Competency Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current L1 River Safety Competence: 2 trips without students or as an observer • NZOIA Canyon Leader A s elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate knowledge of gear and the Mangatepopo River system.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
  ('TL2-31','Meads Wall Traverse',2,'Tongariro','March 2024, version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path The instructor can manage a group on the Meads Wall Traverse. It • Training must be done before assessment, does not cover the competency to rig the traverse not together • Observation can be done by a Senior instructor with the L2 Traverse comp • Assessor must hold NZOIA Rock 2 or equivalent, or Approval from the Training Department. Assessment is by direct observation and questioning. Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current L2 Rock Competence: 2 trips as a co-instructor • NZOIA Rock 2 or Cave 2 A s elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of abseiling gear and equipment.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
  ('TL3-03','Upper Mangatepopo Trip Lead',3,'Tongariro','2024, Version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path The instructor with L3 Upper Mangatepopo Trip Lead Observation can be done by an instructor with L3 competency can: competency including L3 Upper Mangatepopo Trip Lead. Lead and manage groups in the Upper Mangatepopo River, Assessor must hold L3 competency Upper Mangatepopo including upstream to the high point access and down through Trip Lead, assessment is by direct supervision and to be all the jumps above the Mangatepopo Falls abseil. approved by the Training Department Trip Leader must be fully signed off for the competency Note: The Mangatepopo Falls Abseil is listed under L3 Mangatepopo Falls Abseil competency Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current L1 River Safety Competence: Trip Assistant • NZOIA Canyon 1 with at least 4 trips with students as an assistant one trip as an observer or assistant A s elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 3. Demonstrate emergency skills.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
