  ('CL1-08','Bush (Coromandel)',1,'Coromandel','2025, version 1','Scope The L1 bush instructor can: Observations Lead and manage groups on formed and marked tracks, May be done by any Instructor holding easy access to tracks or on strong linear features in the bush Bush (L1) Comp and open terrain This may include minor river crossings or short travel in stream-ways. Assessment Assessor must be an The following are examples of environments that could be • Outdoor Instructor step 2 with within the scope: Bush (L2) with Training ✓ Tracks on our local map that are well defined ie department approval from kiwi lookout to base ✓ River travel up the Tangiaro stream • Or NZOIA Bush 1. ✓ L1 Bush Trips Tongariro Assessment is through discussion and direct observation Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current Competence ❑ No less than 10 days (4 hours duration) experience bush walking ❑ 5 additional days as leader or co-leader in a bush environment. • NZOIA Bush 1 ❑ Local famil of traplines • 15 Logged bush instruction days + Observation A S elf O b s 1 O b s 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate knowledge, care and appropriate use of gear and equipment commonly used.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
  ('CL1-11','Overnight (Coromandel)',1,'Coromandel','2025, version 1','Scope Assessment The L1 instructor can: Observations can be done by anyone Lead and manage groups on in defined campsites in a with the Overnight (L1) Competency. bush/water environments within the local operating area with easy access Assessor must be an The following are examples of environments within the • Outdoor Instructor holding scope: Overnight (L1) with Training department approval ✓ Little acre • or NZOIA Bush 1. ✓ Piwakawaka pools ✓ The grove Assessment is by observation and ✓ Other campsites on property discussion ✓ Waikawau doc campsite ✓ Level 1 campsites Tongariro Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of ❑ No less than 10 nights personal camping Current Competence ❑ 5 additional nights as leader or co-leader ❑ L1 Bush or L1 Summer Alpine or L1 Water competencies • NZOIA Bush One • 10 Logged Instruction overnights + Observation A A S elf O b s S ite 1o r ssess S ite 2 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate knowledge, care and appropriate use of gear and equipment commonly used.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs", "assess1": "Assess site 1", "assess2": "Assess site 2"}',2,false),
  ('CL1-14','Abseiling (Coromandel)',1,'Coromandel','2025, version 1','Scope Assessment • There is well defined access for the participant to the abseil Assessor must be an Outdoor Instructor step 2 and the site allows for simple participant management. and hold • Rock Climbing (L2) and Training • The setup is on pre-arranged anchors Department approval • Or - NZOIA Rock 1, alpine 2 or cave 1. • Personal safety can be set up simply Assessment is by direct observation • The base of the abseil is easy to manage Assessment is site specific. Instructor must demonstrate competence at each site. Instructor must be signed as competent at each site before working solo with a group. Competency is achieved once signed off at a single site but: Sites within the scope may include: The instructor may only operate ✓ Tangiaro Abseil Site( set up only not including bottom unsupervised at sites that have been retrieval) assessed/approved. ✓ L1 sites Tongariro with famil Famil’s may be done by NZOIA Rock 1 or equivalent Internal Competency Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of ❑ Complete at least 10 personal abseils at a variety of sites off their own set-ups Current Competence ❑ no less than 5 additional days as a leader or co-leader assisting with set-up and management • NZOIA Abseil Leader with site famil • 10 Logged Instruction days abseiling + Observation + famils A Site 1: s elf O b s O b s 1 ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of abseiling gear and equipment.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs", "obs2": "Obs 1", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1,false),
